  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes (especially when sentiment is negative or neutral).",
    "Adjust downward if sentiment history shows persistent negative signals (e.g., -0.20 or -0.25) and price is trending upward.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias when true outcome deviates significantly from recent 5-10 day average, especially after high volatility.",
    "Lower forecast for long horizons (e.g., 30d) when sentiment is weak or negative, as market tends to correct downward.",
    "Increase downward bias if recent history shows strong downward momentum (e.g., 3 consecutive days below 70) and sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Avoid overreacting to short-term sentiment spikes — model should not overcorrect or overreact to single-day sentiment shifts."
  ]
}
